    "explicitRoots": 566
  },
  "identityBoundary": "Implementation, ABI, runtime and formal sources are preserved. The exported world, log and small entry frame cell texts of the second call are byte-identical to the received texts of the first FREEZE; the calldata and revert output texts are new raw literals. The world after the revert is the world before the call.",
  "reproductionBoundary": "Full mode rehashes retained source, databases, heap lineage, complete guarded roots, unchanged current inputs and exact single-analysis launch receipts. Metadata mode does not replay proofs. Both modes leave whole engine semantics and final independent Assurance unclaimed.",
  "conditionBoundary": "The theorems hold for every keccak function with values below 2^256 that has the recorded values at the storage slots the first FREEZE reads, with the big-endian word encoding, at the received valuation point (first and second amount 1, the recorded timestamp). TRUST_Returned is the gate label for a kernel-delivered outcome, not the EVM RETURN instruction; the raw status is an EVM revert. The external call list is set empty by the assembler and is not read by the rejection relation. Controls change the command identifier in the report, the status result, the phase, the classifier or the logs.",
  "summaryBoundary": "The symbolic family beyond the received point, engine equivalence, the external call list, the general runtime links, central integration and final Assurance remain incomplete.",
